4. Errors and fixes (most significant, chronologically):
   - React/react-dom version mismatch → synced both to `^19.3.0` in package.json, ran `npm install`.
   - Shift+Z hotkey never fired due to a stale guard (`if (e.shiftKey) return` when it should have required shift) — found and fixed; later the whole feature was replaced per user request with Ctrl+Enter/Ctrl+Shift+Enter.
   - Connector-dot z-index risk: explicitly avoided ever giving `.group`, `.node-connector`, `.resize-handle`, or `.group__drag-handle` any `z-index`, relying entirely on DOM order, because a child z-index would "escape" into the parent stacking context and could render above cards — this constraint is repeated as a comment in the CSS and must be preserved for any future group/card layering work.
   - Curve-routing bug: original perpendicular-bow bezier degenerated to a straight line when both node sides were axis-aligned opposite (e.g. directly stacked top/bottom) — fixed by adding a perpendicular bow component alongside the per-side normal-aligned stubs in `curvedPath` (utils/geometry.js).
   - Menu-position and arrow-position lag when toggling text size — root cause: `getNodeBox`/`selectionMenuAnchor` read DOM `offsetWidth/offsetHeight` which lag one render behind a discrete data change. Fixed by making `getNodeBox` prefer board data (`card.x/y/w`, and `card.h` for big cards) and only fall back to DOM measurement for a regular card's content-driven height.
   - Remaining lag for big→regular text conversion specifically: regular height is DOM-only and has no follow-up state change to trigger a re-render. Fixed via a `ResizeObserver` (`cardResizeObserverRef`) wired into each card's `registerRef`, bumping an inert `bumpLayoutTick` state on any real size change.
   - Safari clipboard-read confirmation popup on `navigator.clipboard.readText()` — switched entirely to native `paste` event + `e.clipboardData.getData('text/plain')`, removing the async API call for that path.
   - Swatch border striping artifact: `.swatch`'s translucent `border-color: var(--border-soft)` blended visibly with the new half/half gradient fill underneath. First attempted `background-clip: padding-box` (user reported "same behavior" — did not fully fix it), then added a dedicated **opaque** `--border-static` CSS variable (`#c7cbd2` light / `#5c6270` dark) and switched `.swatch`'s border to use it — this was the user's own suggested fix ("can the outer ring of the swatch be set to static colors?").
   - Nested-group marquee bug: dragging from within a parent group excluded ALL groups from selection (too broad); fixed to only exclude the specific `clickGroupId` group that the drag started within, letting nested child groups still be selected.
   - Selected-arrow transparency: `.edge__arrowhead--selected` and `.edge--selected .edge__line` used `var(--outline)` (an rgba value) as a solid fill, causing visible background bleed-through; fixed by switching both to `var(--ink)` (opaque).

